      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nvoid body_force(float *restrict px, float *restrict py, float *restrict pz,\n                float *restrict vx, float *restrict vy, float *restrict vz,\n                float dt, int n) {\n  #pragma omp parallel for\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    float fx = 0.0f;\n    float fy = 0.0f;\n    float fz = 0.0f;\n    const float xi = px[i];\n    const float yi = py[i];\n    const float zi = pz[i];\n\n    #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz) aligned(px,py,pz:16)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      float dx = px[j] - xi;\n      float dy = py[j] - yi;\n      float dz = pz[j] - zi;\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n      float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrtf(sqrd_dist);\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    vx[i] += dt*fx;\n    vy[i] += dt*fy;\n    vz[i] += dt*fz;\n  }\n}\n\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  // Allocate SoA arrays with alignment for SIMD\n  float *px, *py, *pz, *vx, *vy, *vz;\n  posix_memalign((void**)&px, 16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&py, 16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&pz, 16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&vx, 16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&vy, 16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  posix_memalign((void**)&vz, 16, nbodies * sizeof(float));\n\n  // Scatter input data into SoA layout\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    px[i] = bodies[i].x;\n    py[i] = bodies[i].y;\n    pz[i] = bodies[i].z;\n    vx[i] = bodies[i].vx;\n    vy[i] = bodies[i].vy;\n    vz[i] = bodies[i].vz;\n  }\n\n  // Free original AoS array after scattering\n  free(bodies);\n\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n    body_force(px, py, pz, vx, vy, vz, DT, nbodies);\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for simd aligned(px,py,pz,vx,vy,vz:16)\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n      px[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n      py[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n      pz[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Gather results back into AoS for output\n  Body *out = (Body *)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    out[i].x = px[i];\n    out[i].y = py[i];\n    out[i].z = pz[i];\n    out[i].vx = vx[i];\n    out[i].vy = vy[i];\n    out[i].vz = vz[i];\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, out);\n\n  free(px); free(py); free(pz);\n  free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n  free(out);\n\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Converting to struct-of-arrays (SoA) with aligned allocation (16-byte), restrict qualifiers, hoisting p[i] reads outside inner loop, and using combined OpenMP parallel for simd reduction on the force computation will improve SIMD vectorization efficiency by providing contiguous memory access per coordinate component. This reduces cache misses and enables wider NEON instructions on ARM64, potentially lowering execution time below previous SoA-based results.",
  "notes": "Candidate uses posix_memalign for alignment, restrict pointers in body_force to avoid aliasing, explicit #pragma omp simd reduction with aligned clause on inner j-loop, and hoists xi,yi,zi. Position update loop also uses parallel for simd aligned. Scatter/gather at I/O boundaries adds O(n) overhead but is negligible compared to simulation time.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Convert AoS (Body struct array) to SoA with separate float arrays",
    "Add restrict qualifiers on force function parameters",
    "Allocate arrays with posix_memalign for 16-byte alignment",
    "Hoist px[i], py[i], pz[i] reads outside inner j-loop into local variables",
    "Apply #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz) aligned on inner loop",
    "Use sqrtf instead of sqrt for single precision",
    "Parallelize outer i-loop with #pragma omp parallel for",
    "Position update uses #pragma omp parallel for simd aligned"
  ]
